{"duration_api_ms":109082,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"edb00253-920e-4ef7-8116-26e734d25346","total_cost_usd":0.41010399999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":46,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26248,"cache_read_input_tokens":973700,"output_tokens":11028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4542},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26248,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2105,"cache_read_input_tokens":49867,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":11028,"cacheReadInputTokens":973700,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26248,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41010399999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":4542,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Hardened /tmp and /dev/shm on node1 (Ubuntu 16.04) with noexec,nosuid,nodev, made it reboot-persistent, and verified both the mount options and functional enforcement (exec denied, device nodes denied) before and after a full node restart with a changed boot ID.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected baseline: /tmp was part of root ext4 fs (no separate mount); /dev/shm was tmpfs with only nosuid,nodev\",\"Backed up /etc/fstab, added a bind-mount fstab entry for /tmp (bind,noexec,nosuid,nodev) and a tmpfs fstab entry for /dev/shm (defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev)\",\"Discovered bind mounts on this system don't apply extra options via a single mount -a pass, so created /etc/systemd/system/tmp-hardening.service (oneshot, After=tmp.mount, Before=local-fs.target, WantedBy=local-fs.target) to remount /tmp with the hardened options at every boot, and enabled it\",\"Applied changes live and verified via findmnt that both /tmp and /dev/shm show rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec\",\"Functionally verified enforcement pre-restart: script execution from /tmp and /dev/shm returned exit 126 (Permission denied), and reading a root-owned mknod'd character device in either mount returned Permission denied\",\"Captured baseline boot_id (1f0657c2-...) and mount state\",\"Triggered a native single-node reboot (systemctl reboot via backgrounded sudo sh -c 'sleep 2; systemctl reboot') so the exec ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed to 4b123f3b-... proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified post-restart: findmnt shows /tmp and /dev/shm still carry noexec,nosuid,nodev; tmp-hardening.service is enabled and active; re-ran the exec and device-node functional tests, both blocked identically to pre-restart\",\"Cleaned up all test artifacts (exectest.sh, testdev nodes) on both mounts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline mount/config state before any changes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fcb09878df7446ec\",\"cmd-0d4e5f3dd8d049c2\"],\"summary\":\"Showed /tmp had no separate mount and /dev/shm lacked noexec before hardening\"},{\"requirement\":\"fstab updated with hardened options for /tmp and /dev/shm\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-118f3638ad904f4c\",\"cmd-1839344bc1824077\"],\"summary\":\"Backed up fstab then appended bind/tmpfs entries with noexec,nosuid,nodev\"},{\"requirement\":\"Discovery that bind mount needs an explicit remount step, and creation of persistent systemd remount unit\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1545ac79c959445f\",\"cmd-adc42335c9874828\",\"cmd-4890788b7fc045ed\",\"cmd-c5f9084551134a25\",\"cmd-7acae9f05ecb446d\"],\"summary\":\"Proved mount -a alone doesn't apply bind options; added and enabled tmp-hardening.service which correctly remounts /tmp with the required flags\"},{\"requirement\":\"Live functional proof that exec, setuid, and device nodes are ignored on /tmp and /dev/shm (pre-restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-93634d7c4af64918\",\"cmd-13ace413dc804a22\"],\"summary\":\"Script execution returned exit 126 on both mounts; device node read returned Permission denied on both mounts (nosuid covered by findmnt option confirmation since noexec already blocks all execution including setuid binaries)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + mount state) for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-571107f722794e74\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 1f0657c2-c163-4ef6-be0b-3118b10aa595 plus findmnt output confirming hardened options and enabled/active service, prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-db2a6d2a31054616\",\"cmd-5879fbb036b64a0c\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded sudo reboot command with a 2s delay; exec call returned REBOOT_TRIGGERED successfully before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof of changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6b9a262272754cbc\",\"cmd-20c5d7f077ef4527\",\"cmd-6e774b637ab84821\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id was unchanged, then connection was refused during reboot, then boot_id returned as 4b123f3b-ec2e-4211-8c68-982213933b4d, a different value confirming an actual restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: hardened mount options persisted and service is healthy\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3fde091f76834de0\"],\"summary\":\"findmnt confirms both /tmp and /dev/shm retain nosuid,nodev,noexec after reboot; tmp-hardening.service is enabled and active (exited 0) post-boot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart functional proof that exec/device restrictions are enforced\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9f48f988da454e67\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, script execution on /tmp and /dev/shm again returned exit 126, and device-node reads again returned Permission denied on both mounts\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Hardened /tmp and /dev/shm on node1 (Ubuntu 16.04) with noexec,nosuid,nodev, made it reboot-persistent, and verified both the mount options and functional enforcement (exec denied, device nodes denied) before and after a full node restart with a changed boot ID.","actions_performed":["Inspected baseline: /tmp was part of root ext4 fs (no separate mount); /dev/shm was tmpfs with only nosuid,nodev","Backed up /etc/fstab, added a bind-mount fstab entry for /tmp (bind,noexec,nosuid,nodev) and a tmpfs fstab entry for /dev/shm (defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev)","Discovered bind mounts on this system don't apply extra options via a single mount -a pass, so created /etc/systemd/system/tmp-hardening.service (oneshot, After=tmp.mount, Before=local-fs.target, WantedBy=local-fs.target) to remount /tmp with the hardened options at every boot, and enabled it","Applied changes live and verified via findmnt that both /tmp and /dev/shm show rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec","Functionally verified enforcement pre-restart: script execution from /tmp and /dev/shm returned exit 126 (Permission denied), and reading a root-owned mknod'd character device in either mount returned Permission denied","Captured baseline boot_id (1f0657c2-...) and mount state","Triggered a native single-node reboot (systemctl reboot via backgrounded sudo sh -c 'sleep 2; systemctl reboot') so the exec ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed to 4b123f3b-... proving an actual restart occurred","Re-verified post-restart: findmnt shows /tmp and /dev/shm still carry noexec,nosuid,nodev; tmp-hardening.service is enabled and active; re-ran the exec and device-node functional tests, both blocked identically to pre-restart","Cleaned up all test artifacts (exectest.sh, testdev nodes) on both mounts"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline mount/config state before any changes","command_ids":["cmd-fcb09878df7446ec","cmd-0d4e5f3dd8d049c2"],"summary":"Showed /tmp had no separate mount and /dev/shm lacked noexec before hardening"},{"requirement":"fstab updated with hardened options for /tmp and /dev/shm","command_ids":["cmd-118f3638ad904f4c","cmd-1839344bc1824077"],"summary":"Backed up fstab then appended bind/tmpfs entries with noexec,nosuid,nodev"},{"requirement":"Discovery that bind mount needs an explicit remount step, and creation of persistent systemd remount unit","command_ids":["cmd-1545ac79c959445f","cmd-adc42335c9874828","cmd-4890788b7fc045ed","cmd-c5f9084551134a25","cmd-7acae9f05ecb446d"],"summary":"Proved mount -a alone doesn't apply bind options; added and enabled tmp-hardening.service which correctly remounts /tmp with the required flags"},{"requirement":"Live functional proof that exec, setuid, and device nodes are ignored on /tmp and /dev/shm (pre-restart)","command_ids":["cmd-93634d7c4af64918","cmd-13ace413dc804a22"],"summary":"Script execution returned exit 126 on both mounts; device node read returned Permission denied on both mounts (nosuid covered by findmnt option confirmation since noexec already blocks all execution including setuid binaries)"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + mount state) for node1","command_ids":["cmd-571107f722794e74"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 1f0657c2-c163-4ef6-be0b-3118b10aa595 plus findmnt output confirming hardened options and enabled/active service, prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-db2a6d2a31054616","cmd-5879fbb036b64a0c"],"summary":"Backgrounded sudo reboot command with a 2s delay; exec call returned REBOOT_TRIGGERED successfully before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity after restart","command_ids":["cmd-6b9a262272754cbc","cmd-20c5d7f077ef4527","cmd-6e774b637ab84821"],"summary":"boot_id was unchanged, then connection was refused during reboot, then boot_id returned as 4b123f3b-ec2e-4211-8c68-982213933b4d, a different value confirming an actual restart"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery: hardened mount options persisted and service is healthy","command_ids":["cmd-3fde091f76834de0"],"summary":"findmnt confirms both /tmp and /dev/shm retain nosuid,nodev,noexec after reboot; tmp-hardening.service is enabled and active (exited 0) post-boot"},{"requirement":"Post-restart functional proof that exec/device restrictions are enforced","command_ids":["cmd-9f48f988da454e67"],"summary":"After reboot, script execution on /tmp and /dev/shm again returned exit 126, and device-node reads again returned Permission denied on both mounts"}]},"ttft_ms":2302,"type":"result","duration_ms":117778,"uuid":"671b041a-d3e8-414b-a98b-4415348b3d7d","ttft_stream_ms":1298,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1299,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
